---
import screenshot from "../assets/outdoor-reflections-page.png";

interface Props {
    title: string;
    gitUrl: string;
    liveUrl?: string;
}

const { title, gitUrl, liveUrl } = Astro.props;
---

<article class="mt-10 sm:mt-14">
    <header>
        <h1 class="font-jersey text-5xl leading-none sm:text-7xl">{title}</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 font-hanken text-lg leading-relaxed text-[#EAE6E3]/85">I built an offline-first editor that saves writing and sketches in the browser and syncs pending edits when the connection returns.</p>
        <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <a class="case-link" href={gitUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View code <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            {liveUrl && (
                <a class="case-link" href={liveUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Try live demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            )}
        </div>
    </header>

    <figure class="mt-8 sm:mt-12">
        <img class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/15" src={screenshot.src} width={screenshot.width} height={screenshot.height} alt="Outdoor Reflections landing page with a sample journal entry containing writing and a sketch" />
        <figcaption>Outdoor Reflections shows writing and sketches together in a single entry.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-10 sm:mt-16 sm:space-y-14">
        <section class="case-section">
            <h2>Problem and scope</h2>
            <p>A connection can disappear while someone is writing or sketching outdoors. I built the editor, local persistence, and sync flow so a saved entry can be reopened on the same device while offline and uploaded later.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="case-section">
            <h2>How it works</h2>
            <p>After a short pause in editing, the browser saves the entry to IndexedDB and marks it as pending. When the connection returns, the sync client sends pending changes to the NestJS API and reconciles the server response with edits still on the device.</p>
            <figure class="mt-5">
                <ol class="sync-flow">
                    <li><strong>Editor</strong><span>Write or sketch</span></li>
                    <li><strong>IndexedDB</strong><span>Save locally</span></li>
                    <li><strong>Sync client</strong><span>Send pending edits</span></li>
                    <li><strong>NestJS API</strong><span>Reconcile with PostgreSQL</span></li>
                </ol>
                <figcaption>The editor saves locally first. Saving to the account happens when sync can run.</figcaption>
            </figure>
        </section>

        <section class="case-section">
            <h2>Engineering decisions</h2>
            <dl class="mt-5 space-y-5">
                <div>
                    <dt>Autosave locally before syncing</dt>
                    <dd>Saving to IndexedDB after a short pause keeps network latency out of the editor. It also makes pending changes explicit so the client can retry after an interruption.</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>Keep drawings as SVG paths</dt>
                    <dd>Each stroke is stored as a path with its colour. That lets drawings scale with the editor and travel in the same entry payload as the writing.</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>Reconcile updates per entry</dt>
                    <dd>The API checks ownership and edit timestamps before applying updates. It reports mixed outcomes so one rejected entry does not discard the rest of the batch.</dd>
                </div>
            </dl>
        </section>

        <section class="case-section">
            <h2>How I verified it</h2>
            <p>I covered several failure cases in the sync tests on the development branch.</p>
            <ul class="verification-list">
                <li>After a deletion syncs, retry both the deletion and an older copy of the entry. The stored deletion marker should remain, with the encrypted content cleared.</li>
                <li>Send a valid encrypted entry and invalid plaintext entries in the same batch. The valid entry should save, and the API should report the rejected entries.</li>
                <li>Deliver an older sync acknowledgement after a local deletion. The deletion should stay pending on the device.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-2">
                <a class="evidence-link" href={`${gitUrl}/blob/dev/backend/src/reflections/sync/sync.service.integration.spec.ts`}>Backend integration tests</a>
                <a class="evidence-link" href={`${gitUrl}/blob/dev/frontend/lib/context/authContext.sync.test.tsx`}>Frontend sync tests</a>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="case-section">
            <h2>Current state</h2>
            <p>The deployed version supports writing and sketching offline, then syncing to an account. The development branch adds browser-side encryption for entry content and tests for encrypted sync and deletion handling.</p>
        </section>
    </div>
</article>

<style>
    @reference "../styles/global.css";

    .case-link {
        @apply inline-flex min-h-9 items-center gap-2 rounded-lg border border-white/20 bg-white/5 px-3 font-hanken text-sm transition-colors hover:border-white/40 hover:bg-white/10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4;
    }

    .case-section {
        @apply border-t border-white/15 pt-5 sm:pt-6;
    }

    .case-section h2 {
        @apply font-jersey text-3xl sm:text-4xl;
    }

    .case-section p,
    .case-section dd,
    .verification-list {
        @apply mt-2 font-hanken text-base leading-relaxed text-[#EAE6E3]/85;
    }

    .case-section dt {
        @apply font-hanken font-semibold;
    }

    figcaption {
        @apply mt-2 font-hanken text-sm text-[#EAE6E3]/65;
    }

    .sync-flow {
        @apply grid grid-cols-2 gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-white/15 bg-white/15 sm:grid-cols-4;
    }

    .sync-flow li {
        @apply flex flex-col gap-1 bg-[#232324] p-3 font-hanken text-sm;
    }

    .sync-flow span {
        @apply text-[#EAE6E3]/75;
    }

    .verification-list {
        @apply list-disc space-y-2 pl-5;
    }

    .evidence-link {
        @apply font-hanken text-sm underline underline-offset-4;
    }
</style>
